racter recognition\n(OCR) if the document contains scanned pages, or direct text extraction for digital PDFs. The extracted text is\nthen cleaned and normalized to remove formatting artifacts.\nNext, the text is split into overlapping chunks using a strategy that preserves semantic coherence. Rather')), (0.01639344262295082, Document(id='5c510ecf-0f27-4a4e-9900-cf6d54414890', metadata={'producer': 'PyPDF', 'page': 0, 'source': 'notebooklm_rag.pdf', 'creationdate': '2026-04-05T09:52:40+00:00', 'page_label': '1', 'total_pages': 3, 'creator': 'PyPDF'}, page_content='How NotebookLM is Performing RAG Under the Hood\n1. Introduction to NotebookLM\nNotebookLM is an AI-powered research and note-taking tool developed by Google. It is designed to help\nusers understand complex documents, generate insights, and answer questions based on content that users\nupload directly. Unlike general-purpose AI assistants, NotebookLM grounds all of its responses in the source')), (0.015873015873015872, Document(id='5a6632c9-80f0-4e29-9fc4-8be0877b33e1', metadata={'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'total_pages': 3, 'source': 'notebooklm_rag.pdf', 'creationdate': '2026-04-05T09:52:40+00:00', 'creator': 'PyPDF', 'producer': 'PyPDF'}, page_content='model can reference the specific chunks it used to generate an answer.\n3. How NotebookLM Processes Documents'))])
